Package: BamScaleR
Type: Package
Title: Bioconductor-Friendly Multithreaded BAM Processing
Version: 0.99.5
Authors@R: c(
    person("Chirag", "Parsania", email = "chirag.parsania@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
  )
Description: BamScaleR reads BAM files using multiple threads per file and
    returns the objects that Bioconductor workflows already use, so it can
    take the place of Rsamtools::scanBam() and
    GenomicAlignments::readGAlignments() in existing analyses. It builds on
    the ompBAM C++ library, which decompresses BAM blocks in parallel, and
    adds readers that select fields like scanBam(), apply the flag,
    mapping-quality and region filters of Rsamtools::ScanBamParam, and return
    a data.frame, DataFrame, scanBam-style list, GAlignments or
    GAlignmentPairs object. It also
    computes common summaries inside the multithreaded reader without
    creating per-read R objects: per-chromosome read counts, paired-end
    fragment-size and mapping-quality distributions, per-base coverage as an
    RleList, and coverage written directly to a bigWig file. Several BAM files
    can additionally be processed in parallel with BiocParallel.
